# Claude Code internals
.claude/

# WaRF state lives in .warf/ (see warf/paths.py), not in the package.
# Tracked on purpose: the session log (the research data the talk's charts are
# generated from), the corpus profile and the talk snapshot. The log is not
# listed here: in a fresh clone an ignore rule would silently keep it out of
# the first commit.
.warf/profiles/*
!.warf/profiles/*snapshot*.json
!.warf/profiles/corpus_v1.json
.warf/debug.log
# A personal preference of this working copy (open the pages in the browser), not project state.
.warf/settings.json

# Experiment runs (tools/run_persona_experiment.py) live apart from the talk
# corpus, so that a refresh of .warf/ always shows the corpus. The sessions and
# profiles there are research data and are meant to be tracked; generated
# dashboards and logs are not.
.warf-experiments/*.html
.warf-experiments/debug.log

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Packaging (pip install -e . / builds)
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Environment / secrets
.env

# LaTeX build output (compile from slides/)
slides/*.aux
slides/*.log
slides/*.nav
slides/*.out
slides/*.snm
slides/*.toc
